  R3: the structural reason the two requirements pull apart.  With f = a (2X)^n and X = e^{-2S}/2,
      B = e^S f = a e^{(1-2n)S}.  IC11 needs n > 1 for the convex pressure to fix the plateau cone; but S
      GROWS along the transition, so B DECAYS by e^{(1-2n) dS} exactly where the inequality needs it to grow.
